// TEST: Floor Kernel Param Dimensioned (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3006
// floor/ceil/log10 have no complex overload, so their scalar arm used to PIN an
// unresolved operand to Float64 -- and inside a lambda body that operand IS the
// kernel param, so the pin bound it to BARE Float64 and erased the element's
// unit before apply-site unification. kernelBodyUnits then re-ran the same
// per-op table against no signature and accepted. `log(d)` in the identical
// spelling always rejected, because the complex intrinsics DEFER instead of
// pinning; the pin is now deferred inside a lambda body too, the same carve-out
// inferBinaryIntrinsic's `pin` makes for atan2/log_base. Scalar position keeps
// the pin (and its eager complex rejection) -- units/020 is the accepting side.
Unit meters
let D: Array<Float<meters> like Idx<3>> = [1.5, 2.5, 3.5]
let bad = (method_for(D) <@> lambda(d) -> floor(d)) |> compute
